arXiv:2507.06567v1 [cs.LG] 09 Jul 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Qian Chen
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Xianhao Chen
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Kaibin Huang
</span><span id="id1" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_correspondence ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Q. Chen, X. Chen, and K. Huang are with the Department of Electrical and
Electronic Engineering, The University of Hong Kong, Hong Kong (Email: qchen@eee.hku.hk, xchen@eee.hku.hk, and huangkb@hku.hk). Corresponding authors: X. Chen and K. Huang.</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models improve the scalability of large language models (LLMs) by activating only a small subset of relevant experts per input. However, the sheer number of expert networks in an MoE model introduces a significant storage burden for an edge device. To address this challenge, we consider a scenario where experts are dispersed within an edge network for distributed inference. Based on the popular Top-<math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection strategy, we formulate a latency minimization problem by optimizing expert caching on edge servers under storage constraints. When <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the problem reduces to a monotone submodular maximization problem with knapsack constraints, for which we design a greedy-based algorithm with a <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation guarantee. For the general case where <math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, expert co-activation within the same MoE layer introduces non-submodularity, causing greedy methods to be ineffective. To tackle this issue, we propose a successive greedy decomposition method to decompose the original problem into a series of subproblems, with each being solved by a dynamic programming approach. Furthermore, we design an accelerated algorithm based on the max-convolution technique to obtain the approximate solution with a provable guarantee in polynomial time. Simulation results on various MoE models demonstrate that our method significantly reduces inference latency compared to existing baselines.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Edge AI, large language models, mixture-of-experts, expert caching, edge inference.

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models (LLMs), such as GPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and LLaMA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, have delivered remarkable performance across various tasks, including many privacy-sensitive and real-time applications <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. Driven by the growing demand for privacy preservation and low-latency responses, there is a pivotal trend toward deploying LLMs at the network edge <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. Reflecting this trend, leading technology companies such as Qualcomm, Huawei, and Apple have already integrated on-device LLMs into consumer-grade mobile devices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. This movement toward edge deployment is expected to shape the future of LLMs and fundamentally transform the landscape of AI-powered mobile applications.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite these advances, LLMs at the network edge face inherent performance limitations compared with the cloud-based counterparts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. This is because the capabilities of LLMs generally scale with model size and computing resources <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, making it challenging to achieve high performance under edge resource constraints. To overcome the scaling challenges, the Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture has emerged as a predominant solution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, which has been adopted in numerous state-of-the-art LLMs such as Phi-3.5-MoE, DeepSeek-V3, and Hunyuan-Large <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Specifically, MoE models replace each <span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">dense</span> transformer block with a massive set of expert networks (e.g., feedforward networks (FFNs)), among which only a subset is activated for each input token, as visualized in Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ I Introduction ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This paradigm allows LLMs to scale in size without a proportional increase in computation for each inference, thereby enabling an effective balance between model performance and computational efficiency – an essential requirement for deployment at the network edge.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, while MoE architectures substantially reduce inference workload, they pose significant <span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">storage</span> challenges for edge devices. For instance, the Switch Transformer architecture allows each MoE layer to host up to hundreds of experts, leading to an MoE model up to 65 times larger than a FLOPs-equivalent dense T5 model, from 446 MB to 29.4 GB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. Such an explosion in parameters makes them ill-suited for edge devices with limited storage capacity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, such as the iPhone 16 with only 128 GB basic storage. In practice, only a small fraction of experts can be cached locally on mobile devices, thereby constraining the scale of MoE models for on-device deployment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Considering that the majority of parameters in MoE models are contributed by expert networks<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          Considering the Switch Transformer model family, when the number of expert networks per MoE layer increases from 8 to 32, the proportion of the MoE model’s total data size occupied by the expert networks rises from 82.3% to 94.4%.</span></span></span>, a natural idea to address the above challenge is to <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">distribute experts across edge networks</span>. Specifically, we envision a scenario where users store only a subset of their preferred experts locally, whereas the wireless edge network caches the remaining experts. The wireless edge network, which can be a 6G mobile network, hosts a massive number of experts for various MoE-based LLMs on distributed edge servers (e.g., base stations). When desired experts are not locally available, users route their token embedding to nearby wireless edge servers with the corresponding experts for inference. This distributed inference framework for MoE models offer several salient advantages: 1) local data and final predictions remain on the user side with privacy benefits, akin to on-device inference, with only intermediate token embeddings uploaded to edge servers; 2) each user only stores minimal, “slim” version of the MoE models with their most frequently used experts, thus substantially reducing local storage and memory costs; 3) Compared with cloud-based MoE systems, edge caching of experts significantly reduce the response time and backbone traffic.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06567v1/0609_fig_expert_layerwise_text_SQA_MoE-LLaVA-Phi2-2.7B-4e.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/96;" width="191" height="96" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>Visualization of activated experts in different MoE layers of the text part in MoE-LLaVA-Phi2-2.7B-4e with Top-2 strategy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> under the Science Question Answering (SQA) dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The paradigm above gives rise to a fundamental research question: <span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the popularity of experts, how can they be optimally placed across distributed storage-constrained edge servers to enable latency-efficient MoE inference?</span> At the first glance, the problem falls into traditional edge caching problems, which determine the placement of content on edge servers based on their content popularity. Nonetheless, key differences exist. In classical content caching or dense model placement, cached items are independently retrievable <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>. In contrast, the activated experts within the same MoE layer exhibit a strong correlation since the model activates <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> experts per input (typically based on the Top-<math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> strategy). In particular, when multiple selected experts at the same layer are colocated on a single server, they require the identical input token embeddings, which can be transmitted only once. As a result, the overall layer latency is no longer a simple linear summation of individual expert latencies. The coupling effect among the selected experts introduces non-submodularity into the optimization problem, making it significantly more challenging. Consequently, existing delay-optimal content placement schemes, which are often based on submodular optimization and greedy procedures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, are no longer effective for MoE placement in terms of theoretical approximation guarantees when <math id="S1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To address the challenging problem, in this paper, we design a di<span id="S1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">s</span>tributed <span id="S1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">l</span>ow-latency <span id="S1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">i</span>nference in <span id="S1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">M</span>oE with expert caching (SlimCaching) framework under Top-<math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> strategy.
Specifically, given the limited storage capacity of edge servers, we aim to determine optimal expert placement strategies that minimize the average inference latency across all users. The main contributions of this work are summarized as follows:</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define a novel expert caching problem tailored for distributed MoE inference. Considering a multi-edge system with cooperative caching between edge devices and edge servers, we formulate a combinatorial optimization problem to minimize the average inference latency subject to storage capacity constraints.
We identify that the resulting problem is a monotone submodular maximization with multiple knapsack constraints when <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and becomes a monotone but non-submodular and non-supermodular maximization problem when <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> due to expert dependencies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the case of <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we develop a greedy-based algorithm that achieves a <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation guarantee. For the more general setting with <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we propose a successive greedy decomposition approach that reformulates the problem into a sequence of subproblems, each solvable via a dynamic programming (DP)-based algorithm. The proposed algorithm attains a <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\kappa_{g})/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\kappa_{g})/2</annotation></semantics></math>-approximate global solution in polynomial time, where <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is the supermodular curvature. Furthermore, we propose an accelerated algorithm considering the uniform expert sizes within each MoE model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct extensive experiments on SQA and Visual Question Answering (VQA)-v2 datasets using diverse MoE models with varying Top-<math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> configurations. The results demonstrate that the proposed method consistently outperforms traditional greedy baselines in terms of both latency and computational efficiency.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The rest of this paper is organized as follows. We review the related works in Section <a href="#S2" title="II Related Works ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>. Then, we provide the system models in Section <a href="#S3" title="III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, including the expert activation procedure during MoE inference, expert caching model, and per-token inference latency. Based on the activation probability of experts, we formulate a latency-minimization optimization problem and characterize its structural property in Section <a href="#S4" title="IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>. In Section <a href="#S5" title="V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a>, we develop the algorithms for the special case <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> and for the general case <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Experimental results are presented in Section <a href="#S6" title="VI Experimental Results ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI</span></a>, followed by concluding remarks in Section <a href="#S7" title="VII Conclusion Remarks ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Related Works</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The relevant research works on MoE and its edge deployment can be summarized as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1) <span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expert selection</span>:
For MoE-based models, expert selection plays a central role in determining both inference latency and accuracy. The most popular method is Top-<math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection, where, for each input, the <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> experts with the highest routing probabilities are chosen to process the data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. There are also dynamic expert selection strategies, where a threshold is defined such that experts are selected if the cumulative routing probabilities exceed the threshold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. In this work, we adopt the widely used Top-<math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection to study the expert placement problem in edge networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2) In-memory expert caching:</span> One of the main bottlenecks in MoE inference arises from the high memory overhead associated with storing a large number of expert networks. One usual practice is on-demand expert fetching, where inactive experts are kept in low-tier memory and only loaded into GPU memory when selected. However, since the router must first determine the Top-<math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> experts before initiating expert loading, the fetching process is fully serialized with computation, causing substantial latency. To address this issue, an expert prefetching mechanism is developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, where a transformer-based routing path predictor is trained offline to predict expert activation for each input token in a single pass. The predicted experts are then prefetched during the computation of previous layers. Furthermore, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, by decoupling the gating router from the MoE architecture, tokens with similar activation patterns can be grouped into micro-batches, further reducing fetching latency.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3) <span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In-network expert caching:</span> Due to the huge sizes and computation burden, experts sometimes can be distributed over edge networks. By considering task relevance and wireless channel conditions, an energy-aware expert selection framework is developed, where experts are dispersed in wireless edge networks for distributed inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. In this work, however, we focus on expert placement in edge networks based on the widely used Top-<math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection mechanism. To our best knowledge, the expert placement problem has not been investigated in the literature.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Expert placement is a key problem for in-network expert caching, i.e., which experts should be placed on which edge server. While caching has been extensively investigated in areas such as content delivery and model caching, expert caching in MoE models exhibits unique characteristics that render existing solutions inapplicable. In content caching, most prior work assumes independence among content items <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, and the objective is typically to maximize a submodular utility function subject to matroid constraints <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>. This setting enables the application of classical greedy algorithms with a well-known <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation guarantee. In cases where dependencies exist, such as in caching interdependent tasks modeled by directed acyclic graphs, content placement decisions are often made sequentially, with each task requiring a single function to be cached and executed <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>.
In model caching, a recent approach, TrimCaching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, exploits parameter sharing across AI models to improve storage efficiency. By treating model layers as cacheable units, the caching problem can be formulated as a supermodular maximization problem under multiple knapsack constraints.
However, it assumes that a cached model is stored in its entirety, which is infeasible in the context of large-scale MoE models due to their considerable parameter sizes. Expert caching in MoE models poses fundamentally different challenges due to the Top-<math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert activation mechanism, which introduces two key difficulties:
1) <span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Non-submodularity due to expert co-activation:</span>
When <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, multiple experts must be activated simultaneously for each token, leading to strong co-activation dependencies among experts.
The dependency causes the submodularity and supermodularity properties, which are commonly exploited in existing caching formulations, to fail to provide theoretical approximation guarantees in our expert placement problem.
<span id="S2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2) Knapsack-type storage constraints:</span>
Expert caching is further complicated by the heterogeneity in expert sizes across different MoE models. Unlike the commonly assumed cardinality or matroid constraints, the expert caching problem introduces knapsack-type constraints that depend on the data size of cached experts. The above properties necessitate new problem formulations and optimization strategies for expert caching for distributed MoE inference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">System Model</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we consider an MoE-based edge caching system with a set <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=\left\{1,\ldots,N\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=\left\{1,\ldots,N\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> of edge servers and a set <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\left\{1,\ldots,U\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\left\{1,\ldots,U\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> of users.
The storage capacity of edge server <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Edge servers can communicate with each other directly via backhaul links and are also connected to the central cloud (expert model library) with a wired backhaul link.
Each user connects to its nearest edge server and generates a task that requires an MoE architecture for inference, where <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u,m}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability of user <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> requesting model <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> requested MoE models, and the set of models is denoted by <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\left\{1,\ldots,M\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\left\{1,\ldots,M\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For model <math id="S3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the Top-<math id="S3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection mechanism, where <math id="S3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of activated experts within an MoE layer.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Preliminaries: Expert Activation During MoE Inference</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first briefly introduce the preliminaries of MoE inference. Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ III-A Preliminaries: Expert Activation During MoE Inference ‣ III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the architecture of an MoE model.
For MoE model <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of MoE layers is <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, indexed by a set <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{m}=\left\{1,\ldots,L_{m}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{m}=\left\{1,\ldots,L_{m}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each MoE layer consists of a <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gate network</span> and a set of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">expert networks</span> (i.e., FFNs), and the data size of a single expert is denoted by <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the total number of experts is given by <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}L_{m}E_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}L_{m}E_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the set of experts within model <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s MoE layer <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06567v1/fig_MoE_procedure.svg" id="S3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:143/187;" width="143" height="187"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Illustration of an MoE architecture with <math id="S3.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> expert networks in each MoE layer. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We take model <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> as an example to illustrate how expert(s) are activated at MoE layer <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the token-to-expert affinity scores of an input <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, which represents the probability of the token selecting an expert for processing. Then, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)=\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\mathbf{W}_{r}\mathbf{s}^{\mathrm{T}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)=\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\mathbf{W}_{r}\mathbf{s}^{\mathrm{T}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the router parameter. With Top-<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> routing strategy, the experts with <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> highest scores will be activated. Then, the probability of expert <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> can be normalized as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathbf{g}}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}=\begin{cases}\frac{{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}}{\sum_{i^{\prime}\in\mathrm{Top}K_{m}\left({\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)\right)}{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i^{\prime}}},&amp;\text{ if }i\in{\mathrm{Top}}K_{m}\left({\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)\right),\\
0,&amp;\text{ otherwise. }\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext> otherwise. </mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathbf{g}}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}=\begin{cases}\frac{{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}}{\sum_{i^{\prime}\in\mathrm{Top}K_{m}\left({\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)\right)}{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i^{\prime}}},&amp;\text{ if }i\in{\mathrm{Top}}K_{m}\left({\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)\right),\\
0,&amp;\text{ otherwise. }\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Subsequently, the final output of the expert networks can be obtained by <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)=\sum_{i\in{\mathcal{E}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}{\bar{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}y_{i}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)=\sum_{i\in{\mathcal{E}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}{\bar{\mathbf{g}}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)_{i}y_{i}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\left(\mathbf{s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is the output result of the selected expert <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the collection of all possible expert index sets of size <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> that can be activated in MoE layer <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}=\left\{S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\mid\left|S_{m}\right|=K_{m}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}=\left\{S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\mid\left|S_{m}\right|=K_{m}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For example, when <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and there are 3 experts in MoE layer <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}=\left\{\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\},\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},3_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\},\left\{2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},3_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}=\left\{\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\},\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},3_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\},\left\{2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},3_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> and one possible value of <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{1_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)},2_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expert Caching Model</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given that expert networks account for the majority of MoE model’s parameters, we assume that all components of MoE models except the experts are deployed on users, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ III-B Expert Caching Model ‣ III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. This strategy ensures raw input data and final predictions remain on the user side, thereby enhancing user privacy. Due to storage limitations, users can only store a limited number of experts in an MoE model. When the requested experts are not locally available, the user should send the token embeddings to edge servers with cached experts for inference. When the requested experts are not cached at any edge server, the user should send token embeddings to the cloud, which is assumed to cache all experts. After the requested experts complete processing, the nodes send the output results back to the user. Then, the processing of the next MoE layer begins.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06567v1/system_model_multiserver.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/97;" width="229" height="97" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span>A distributed wireless system for MoE inference, where users and edge servers have expert caching capabilities. (a) Illustration of local cache hit, edge cache hit, and edge cache miss. (b) Operations and protocol of SlimCaching within an MoE layer.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we consider that experts on users are pre-determined according to user preference (e.g., their most frequently used experts), whereas the placement of experts in edge networks should be optimized according to user requests and network status.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expert caching state of the users. If the expert with index <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> of MoE model <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s layer <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is pre-cached on user <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> holds; otherwise, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the caching decision variable for the edge servers, with <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> indicating the expert with index <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> of MoE model <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s layer <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is placed at edge server <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Per-token Inference Latency</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{u,n}^{\rm{UL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{u,n}^{\rm{UL}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expected data rate from user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to its associated (nearest) edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{u,n_{u}}^{\rm{UL}}=B_{u}\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{P_{u,n_{u}}G_{u,n_{u}}d_{u,n_{u}}^{-\alpha}}{N_{0}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{u,n_{u}}^{\rm{UL}}=B_{u}\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{P_{u,n_{u}}G_{u,n_{u}}d_{u,n_{u}}^{-\alpha}}{N_{0}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the bandwidth occupied by user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{u,n_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{u,n_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transmit power from user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{u,n_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{u,n_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the uplink antenna-related factor, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u,n_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u,n_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the distance between user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the path-loss coefficient, and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the noise power. Similarly, the downlink achievable rate from the edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> to user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{u,n_{u}}^{\rm{DL}}=B_{u}\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{P_{n_{u},u}G_{n_{u},u}d_{u,n_{u}}^{-\alpha}}{N_{0}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mi>DL</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{u,n_{u}}^{\rm{DL}}=B_{u}\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{P_{n_{u},u}G_{n_{u},u}d_{u,n_{u}}^{-\alpha}}{N_{0}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n_{u},u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n_{u},u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transmit power from edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> to user <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n_{u},u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n_{u},u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the downlink antenna-related factor.
For the backhaul transmissions,
let <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the transmission rate from edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,\mathrm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,\mathrm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the transmission rate from edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to the cloud.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When performing MoE inference, the output tensor preserves the same dimensions as the input tensor. Thus, when using MoE model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> for task inference, the uplink and downlink have identical data transmission sizes, i.e., the size of token embedding denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. When using model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> for inference, given the uplink data rate in (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In III-C Per-token Inference Latency ‣ III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the communication latency of transmitting a token embedding from user <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to its associated edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\rm{UL}}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{u,n_{u}}^{\mathrm{UL}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\rm{UL}}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{u,n_{u}}^{\mathrm{UL}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the communication latency of transmitting a token embedding via the downlink between user <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, via backhaul link from edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and via backhaul link from edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to the cloud can be expressed as <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\rm{DL}}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{u,n_{u}}^{\mathrm{DL}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>DL</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mi>DL</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\rm{DL}}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{u,n_{u}}^{\mathrm{DL}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n,n^{\prime},m}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{n,n^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n,n^{\prime},m}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{n,n^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n,{\mathrm{C}},m}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{n,{\mathrm{C}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n,{\mathrm{C}},m}=\frac{D_{m}}{R_{n,{\mathrm{C}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the computation workload (in FLOPs) of an expert in model <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be calculated according to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>. Let
<math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> be the computing capability (in FLOP/s) of user <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, and the allocated computing capability for each expert denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dot{C}}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dot{C}}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dot{C}}_{u}=C_{u}/E_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dot{C}}_{u}=C_{u}/E_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the local computing latency of user <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> utilizing the expert network of model <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{u}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}E_{m}}{C_{u}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{u}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}E_{m}}{C_{u}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the allocated computing capability for each expert at the edge server and at the cloud, respectively.
In the considered scenario, the users’ request traffic load is sufficiently low, such that computing resource contention among users is not considered.
Thus, the computing latency of the edge server and the cloud utilizing the expert network of model <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> can be given by <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{E},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{E}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>E</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{E},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{E}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{C},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{C},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}=\frac{\mu_{m}^{\mathrm{CP}}}{{\dot{C}}_{\mathrm{C}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Consider that the bottleneck of MoE inference in distributed wireless networks is the communication overhead of inter-nodes, and the delay of token routing to the cloud is much longer than that to edge networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. Thus, the order in which user <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>’s token searches for expert processing is as follows: local user, associated (nearest) edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, other non-associated edge servers <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, and finally the cloud. Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ III-C Per-token Inference Latency ‣ III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows four different cases of token routing when a user requests the expert pair <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i_{m}^{\ell},j_{m}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i_{m}^{\ell},j_{m}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> under Top-2 strategy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.06567v1/fig_4case.png" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/84;" width="215" height="84" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Different cases of token routing when <math id="S3.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Consider an arbitrary user, say <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, requires an expert (group) <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> in the MoE layer <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> for inference. Next, we will discuss the per-token inference latency when traversing this layer.
The number of activated experts at different nodes can be calculated as follows.</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the local user <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, there are <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the associated edge server <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(1-\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)x_{n_{u},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(1-\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)x_{n_{u},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the cloud, there are <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\sum_{i\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(1-\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\prod_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\left(1-x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}=\sum_{i\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(1-\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\prod_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\left(1-x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At other edge servers excluding the associated edge server, there are <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=K_{m}-\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}-\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}-\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>OE</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=K_{m}-\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}-\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}-\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts in total.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For the non-associated edge servers <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote whether it provides processing with its cached expert <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> for user <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\leq x_{n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\leq x_{n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds since edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can provide inference only if it caches the requested expert. Then, the total number of utilized experts at the non-associated edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=\sum_{n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}}\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>OE</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=\sum_{n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}}\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,n^{\prime},i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined in a way that leads to the lowest per-token inference latency, which can be easily obtained given expert placement decisions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that tokens are transmitted sequentially between the associated edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and other edge servers. As a result, <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>OE</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=\sum_{n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}}&amp;\left[{\mathbb{I}\left({{\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}&gt;0}\right)\left({{T_{{n_{u}},n^{\prime},m}}+T_{{\mathrm{E}},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}}\right)}\right.\\
&amp;\left.+{\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}{T_{n^{\prime},{n_{u}},m}}\right].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>OE</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}=\sum_{n^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\setminus n_{u}}&amp;\left[{\mathbb{I}\left({{\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}&gt;0}\right)\left({{T_{{n_{u}},n^{\prime},m}}+T_{{\mathrm{E}},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}}\right)}\right.\\
&amp;\left.+{\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}{T_{n^{\prime},{n_{u}},m}}\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In a special case where <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the token only requires one expert in each MoE layer for processing. In this case, <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{(\ell)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{(\ell)}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{(\ell)}}&amp;=\left(1-\rho_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\left(1-x_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\\
&amp;\cdot\mathop{\prod}\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}n^{\prime\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\\
T_{n_{u},n^{\prime\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime\prime},n_{u},m}\\
&lt;T_{n_{u},n^{\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime},n_{u},m}\end{subarray}}\left(1-x_{n^{\prime\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)x_{n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\beta_{u,n^{\prime},S_{m}^{(\ell)}}&amp;=\left(1-\rho_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\left(1-x_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\\
&amp;\cdot\mathop{\prod}\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}n^{\prime\prime}\in\mathcal{N}\\
T_{n_{u},n^{\prime\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime\prime},n_{u},m}\\
&lt;T_{n_{u},n^{\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime},n_{u},m}\end{subarray}}\left(1-x_{n^{\prime\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)x_{n^{\prime},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">That is, expert <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> is cached at edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all other edge servers <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime\prime}\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime\prime}\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> that provide a lower round-trip transmission latency between <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{u},n^{\prime\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime\prime},n_{u},m}&lt;T_{n_{u},n^{\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime},n_{u},m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{u},n^{\prime\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime\prime},n_{u},m}&lt;T_{n_{u},n^{\prime},m}+T_{n^{\prime},n_{u},m}</annotation></semantics></math>) do not cache this expert. Therefore, the token from user <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is transmitted to edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for processing.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Let us get back to the general case. Based on (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In III-C Per-token Inference Latency ‣ III System Model ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the latency experienced by a token at the edge servers denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}=\mathbb{I}\left(\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}&gt;0\right)T_{\mathrm{E},m}^{\mathrm{CP}}+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>OE</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}=\mathbb{I}\left(\beta_{u,n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}&gt;0\right)T_{\mathrm{E},m}^{\mathrm{CP}}+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{OE}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, the latency from the associated edge server <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> to the cloud denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}&amp;=\mathbb{I}\left({{\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}&gt;0}\right)\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\mathrm{C},m}}+T_{{\mathrm{C}},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}}\right)\\
&amp;+{\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}T_{\mathrm{C},{n_{u}},m}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}&amp;=\mathbb{I}\left({{\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}&gt;0}\right)\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\mathrm{C},m}}+T_{{\mathrm{C}},m}^{{\mathrm{CP}}}}\right)\\
&amp;+{\beta_{u,\mathrm{C},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}}T_{\mathrm{C},{n_{u}},m}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p">As a result, when the local experts cannot satisfy the inference requests, we can obtain the inference latency requiring outer nodes denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>out</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows,</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}&amp;=T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{UL}}+\left(K_{m}-\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{DL}}\\
&amp;+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>out</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>DL</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}&amp;=T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{UL}}+\left(K_{m}-\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{DL}}\\
&amp;+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{E}}+T_{n_{u},S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{C}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the per-token inference latency when user <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> requests expert(s) <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> for inference can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{token}}=\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}T_{u}^{\rm{CP}}+\left(1-\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>out</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{token}}=\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}T_{u}^{\rm{CP}}+\left(1-\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">III-D</span> </span><span id="S3.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Activation Probability and Average Latency</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As analyzed in Section <a href="#S1" title="I Introduction ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>, when using different MoE models, each token will have a unique distribution of activation expert paths.
Let <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability of user <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> selecting expert(s) <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> in model <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s MoE layer <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> for processing, which can be measured by historical statistics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}=\left\{S_{m,j}^{(1)},\dots,S_{m,j}^{(L_{m})}\right\}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}=\left\{S_{m,j}^{(1)},\dots,S_{m,j}^{(L_{m})}\right\}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th path when selecting model <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> for inference, where <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the activated expert(s) in the <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th MoE layer. The probability of each individual path <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> for user <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}</annotation></semantics></math>, can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}&amp;=p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(1)},\dots,S_{m,j}^{(L_{m})}\right)\\
&amp;=p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(1)}\right)\prod_{\ell=2}^{L_{m}}p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\mid S_{m,j}^{(1)},\ldots,S_{m,j}^{(\ell-1)}\right),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}&amp;=p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(1)},\dots,S_{m,j}^{(L_{m})}\right)\\
&amp;=p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(1)}\right)\prod_{\ell=2}^{L_{m}}p_{u}\left(S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\mid S_{m,j}^{(1)},\ldots,S_{m,j}^{(\ell-1)}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is derived from the transition probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{T}}_{u,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{T}}_{u,m}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the average per-token inference latency when user <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> requires model <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\bar{T}}_{u,m}&amp;=\sum_{{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}}p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}\sum_{S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}T_{u,S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\bar{T}}_{u,m}&amp;=\sum_{{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}}p_{u,{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}\sum_{S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{S}}_{m,j}}T_{u,S_{m,j}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the second equation is derived based on the characteristics of joint probability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation and Characterization</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first formulate an optimization problem to minimize the average inference latency subject to the storage capacity constraints. Then, we identify and characterize the structural properties of the optimization problem under different <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Formulation</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the latency reduction function as</p>
<table id="S4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)\triangleq T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\max}-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left({\mathbf{X}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)\triangleq T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\max}-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left({\mathbf{X}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\max}=\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}T_{u}^{\rm{CP}}+\left(1-\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out},\max}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>out</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\max}=\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}T_{u}^{\rm{CP}}+\left(1-\prod_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out},\max},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which denotes the maximal per-token inference latency when user <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> requests the expert(s) <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The term <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>out</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the worst-case latency when the required experts that are not cached locally are also unavailable at any edge server, and thus the token must be processed at the cloud. <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>out</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}&amp;=T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{UL}}+T_{n_{u},{\mathrm{C}},m}+T_{\mathrm{C},m}^{\mathrm{CP}}\\
&amp;+\left(K_{m}-\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\left(T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{DL}}+T_{{\mathrm{C}},n_{u},m}\right).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>out</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>UL</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>DL</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}T_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}^{\mathrm{out,max}}&amp;=T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{UL}}+T_{n_{u},{\mathrm{C}},m}+T_{\mathrm{C},m}^{\mathrm{CP}}\\
&amp;+\left(K_{m}-\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\rho_{u,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\right)\left(T_{u,n_{u},m}^{\mathrm{DL}}+T_{{\mathrm{C}},n_{u},m}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To optimize the expert caching for efficient MoE inference, we aim to minimize the average latency of all generated tokens.
Therefore, the objective function <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=\frac{1}{U}\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}p_{u,m}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>U</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=\frac{1}{U}\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}p_{u,m}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and the optimization problem can be formulated as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E19.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1:\;\max_{\mathbf{X}}\;F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1:\;\max_{\mathbf{X}}\;F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E19.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{s.t.}}\;\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}b_{m}\leq Q_{n},\;\forall n\in\mathcal{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{s.t.}}\;\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}b_{m}\leq Q_{n},\;\forall n\in\mathcal{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E19.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\left\{0,1\right\},\forall n\in\mathcal{N},m\in\mathcal{M},\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\left\{0,1\right\},\forall n\in\mathcal{N},m\in\mathcal{M},\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where Constraint (<a href="#S4.E19.2" title="In 19 ‣ IV-A Problem Formulation ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19b</span></a>) is a knapsack constraint denoting that the cached experts within any edge server cannot exceed its storage capacity, and Constraint (<a href="#S4.E19.3" title="In 19 ‣ IV-A Problem Formulation ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19c</span></a>) denotes that the variable <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}=\left\{x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\mid\forall n\in\mathcal{N},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=\left\{x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\mid\forall n\in\mathcal{N},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of binary variables.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Characterization</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the cooperation of multiple edge servers and the correlation of activated experts, there is a complex coupling relationship within the decision variable, making <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> challenging to solve.
In this subsection, we examine the properties of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> and perform problem mappings, providing a basis for the algorithm design in the next section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define the following ground set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\{\underbrace{v_{1}^{1},\ldots,v_{E}^{1}}_{V_{1}},\ldots,\underbrace{v_{1}^{N},\ldots,v_{E}^{N}}_{V_{N}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></munder><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\{\underbrace{v_{1}^{1},\ldots,v_{E}^{1}}_{V_{1}},\ldots,\underbrace{v_{1}^{N},\ldots,v_{E}^{N}}_{V_{N}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an abstract element denoting the caching state of expert <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at the edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Submodular Function)<span id="Thmdefinition1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Defined over a finite set <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, a set function <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:2^{V}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:2^{V}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be submodular when for every subset <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(X\right)+f\left(Y\right)\geq f\left(X\cup Y\right)+f\left(X\cap Y\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(X\right)+f\left(Y\right)\geq f\left(X\cup Y\right)+f\left(X\cap Y\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Alternatively, defining <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(x|X\right)=f\left(X\cup x\right)-f\left(X\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(x|X\right)=f\left(X\cup x\right)-f\left(X\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as the marginal gain obtained by incorporating item <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> into the set <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, submodularity can equivalently be characterized by the diminishing returns property: for any <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq Y\subset V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq Y\subset V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\setminus Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\setminus Y</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(v|X)\geq f(v|Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(v|X)\geq f(v|Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Supermodular Function)<span id="Thmdefinition2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A set function <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:2^{V}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:2^{V}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be supermodular if the function <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-f</annotation></semantics></math> is submodular. That is, for every <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that: <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)+f(Y)\leq f(X\cup Y)+f(X\cap Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)+f(Y)\leq f(X\cup Y)+f(X\cap Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Equivalently, <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is supermodular if it satisfies the increasing returns property: for all <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq Y\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq Y\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V\setminus Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V\setminus Y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(v\mid X)\leq f(v\mid Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(v\mid X)\leq f(v\mid Y)</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For Top-<math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> strategy, when <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotone non-decreasing submodular maximization problem with <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> knapsack constraints.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Monotonicity is evident since the addition of a new expert placement cannot decrease the value of the objective function <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we show the submodularity or supermodularity of the function.
First, we prove the submodularity of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all MoE models holds. In this case, the probabilities of a user activating different experts within the same layer are independent.
Since the summation of submodular functions preserves submodularity, we only need to demonstrate that the set function <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is submodular for a user <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and an expert <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer.
Consider two caching strategy sets, <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}\subset\hat{X}\subset V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}\subset\hat{X}\subset V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is the ground set which has been defined before. Under the caching strategy <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, user <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> transmits its token to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}\leq{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}\leq{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, indicating that the round-trip transmission latency between edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is lower than that between <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, when <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{n}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, the round-trip transmission latency between edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{n}</annotation></semantics></math> or between <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is 0.
Suppose we add an expert <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in V\setminus\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in V\setminus\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to the edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we discuss the following two cases:</span></p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}&gt;{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}&gt;{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}</annotation></semantics></math>:
In this case, the marginal value satisfies of caching strategy <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}&lt;{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}&lt;{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the marginal value of caching strategy <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> remains zero. If <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}&gt;{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}&gt;{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the marginal value of <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}&lt;{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}+T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}&lt;{{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}</annotation></semantics></math>: In this case, the marginal value of strategy <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The marginal value of strategy <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}+T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},n,m}}-T_{n,{n_{u}},m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the difference in marginal gains between <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left(S_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}-T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}\right)\leq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{u,S_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\left({{T_{{n_{u}},\hat{n},m}}+T_{\hat{n},{n_{u}},m}}-{{T_{{n_{u}},\dot{n},m}}-T_{\dot{n},{n_{u}},m}}\right)\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotone non-decreasing non-submodular non-supermodular
maximization problem with <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> knapsack constraints.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to show that monotonicity holds, which is the same as the case of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For non-submodularity and non-supermodularity, we first take <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=2</annotation></semantics></math> as an example, and then extend this property to a more general case for any <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider two caching strategy sets, <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}\subset\hat{X}\subset V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}\subset\hat{X}\subset V</annotation></semantics></math>, and introduce an expert <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to the set <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\setminus\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\setminus\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Different from <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the activated experts appear in pairs when <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the introduction of any expert will affect the latency when requesting the expert pairs involving this expert.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ IV-B Problem Characterization ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the caching strategy after introducing a new expert <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to the sets <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we assume that the round-trip transmission latency between edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>) and edge servers <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> are in an increasing order.
For simplicity, we assume that for model <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th MoE layer,
the experts except <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> can only be found at the cloud. Also, only the users covered by the edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> require <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}=\left\{i_{m}^{(\ell)},j_{m}^{(\ell)}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}=\left\{i_{m}^{(\ell)},j_{m}^{(\ell)}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> for inference.
In this case, introducing <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> will only impact the latency when users covered by <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> require <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we only need to discuss the property of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}r_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and then obtain the property of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06567v1/fig_set_K2_super.png" id="S4.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/55;" width="224" height="55" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="S4.F5.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{\mathbf{X}}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{\mathbf{X}}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">&gt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{\mathbf{X}}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{\mathbf{X}}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06567v1/fig_set_K2_sub.png" id="S4.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/56;" width="224" height="56" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="S4.F5.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{\mathbf{X}}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{\mathbf{X}}\right)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{\mathbf{X}}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{\mathbf{X}}\right)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>Different relationships between the marginal values of <math id="S4.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we discuss the case in Fig. <a href="#S4.F5.sf1" title="In Fig. 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ IV-B Problem Characterization ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(a)</span></a>.
In order to minimize the E2E latency, for the set <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the token will be transmitted to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B,C\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, before and after adding <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
For the set <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the token will be transmitted to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B,D\}</annotation></semantics></math>, before and after adding <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The marginal values of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(T_{A,C,m}+T_{C,A,m}-T_{B,A,m}+T_{{\rm{E}},m}^{\rm{CP}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(T_{A,C,m}+T_{C,A,m}-T_{B,A,m}+T_{{\rm{E}},m}^{\rm{CP}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}(T_{A,C,m}+T_{C,A,m}-T_{A,B,m}-T_{B,A,m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}(T_{A,C,m}+T_{C,A,m}-T_{A,B,m}-T_{B,A,m})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In this case, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and then <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we discuss the scenario in Fig. <a href="#S4.F5.sf2" title="In Fig. 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ IV-B Problem Characterization ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(b)</span></a>.
For the set <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, before and after adding <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the token will be processed at edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> to minimize the E2E latency. Thus, the marginal value of <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by
<math id="S4.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the set <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the token will be transmitted to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, before and after adding <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> to edge server <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The marginal values of <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}(T_{A,D,m}+T_{D,A,m}-T_{C,A,m}+T_{{\rm{E}},m}^{\rm{CP}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>CP</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)=p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}(T_{A,D,m}+T_{D,A,m}-T_{C,A,m}+T_{{\rm{E}},m}^{\rm{CP}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and then <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds. At this point, when <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we verify that <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is either positive or negative, leading to the property of non-submodularity and non-supermodularity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we extend this property to a more general case for <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. The sketch proof is as follows: the expert <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ IV-B Problem Characterization ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> is replaced by all the required experts excluding <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the expert group including experts <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{(\ell)}\setminus j_{m}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{(\ell)}\setminus j_{m}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. With a similar method to the case <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we can prove that <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\hat{X}\right)-F\left(j_{m}^{(\ell)}\mid\dot{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> may also be either positive or negative.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, when <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the non-submodularity and non-supermodularity always hold for <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Proposed Algorithms</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the structural analysis of <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> under different values of <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in the previous section, we divide the algorithmic discussion into two parts: one for the special case of <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the other for the general case of <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The special case <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> is suitable for the Switch Transformer (ST) family, such as ST-based-X with <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{8,16,32,64,128\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{8,16,32,64,128\}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> and Hash
Layer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.
The general case <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> applies to
GShard and MoE-LLaVA family <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> with the Top-2 strategy and DBRX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> with the Top-4 strategy. In both cases, we will develop approximate algorithms with provable guarantees. Note that the algorithms for the general case <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> can obviously achieve an approximation guarantee to the special case <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, albeit with a slightly weaker approximation ratio compared to the algorithm designed for <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Special Case: <math id="S5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math></span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the objective function of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in the special case.
Let <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{X}}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{X}}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the optimal solution of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}\left(\mathbf{X}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span>1 </span>Algorithm design</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the optimization problem <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> is a submodular maximization problem with knapsack constraints, we can utilize the greedy-based algorithm to obtain the solutions, as shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-A1 Algorithm design ‣ V-A Special Case: K=1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Greedy</span>-based Algorithm When <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Ground set <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, objective function <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, model <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>’s expert data size <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of edge servers <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, storage capacities <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Expert caching results <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> (and the way it is cached).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              Let <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\left\{S_{1},\ldots,S_{N}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\left\{S_{1},\ldots,S_{N}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> be its partition into <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> edge servers.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\setminus S\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\setminus S\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and there exists <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i\in S_{n}}b_{i}\leq Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i\in S_{n}}b_{i}\leq Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}=\arg\max_{i\in V\setminus S}\frac{F_{1}(i\mid S)}{b_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}=\arg\max_{i\in V\setminus S}\frac{F_{1}(i\mid S)}{b_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=S+i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=S+i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=S_{n}+i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=S_{n}+i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\left\{S_{1},\ldots,S_{N}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\left\{S_{1},\ldots,S_{N}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-A1 Algorithm design ‣ V-A Special Case: K=1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> returns a expert caching set <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}\left(S\right)\geq\left(1-1/e\right)F_{1}\left({\mathbf{X}}^{\ast}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}\left(S\right)\geq\left(1-1/e\right)F_{1}\left({\mathbf{X}}^{\ast}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows the approach in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span>2 </span>Computational complexity</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-A1 Algorithm design ‣ V-A Special Case: K=1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is developed from greedy Algorithm, its computational complexity is given by <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-A1 Algorithm design ‣ V-A Special Case: K=1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N^{2}E^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N^{2}E^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">General Case: <math id="S5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we extend our discussion to the general case where both <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> strategies are involved.
Recall that for <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective function of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> is neither submodular nor supermodular, making it challenging to solve. To address this, we first decompose the original problem <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> subproblems and solve them successively in the order of edge server index. Based on the analysis of each subproblem, we demonstrate why the greedy algorithm—effective in the special case—fails to provide a constant approximation ratio in the general case. Leveraging the structure of each subproblem, we then propose a dynamic programming (DP)-based algorithm and also an accelerated algorithm to obtain solutions with a constant approximation guarantee. A detailed discussion of the proposed algorithms and their performance is also provided.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>1 </span>Problem decomposition</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The subproblem of edge server <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as follows.</p>
<table id="S5.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E20.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E20.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}:\;\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}\;{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}:\;\max_{\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}\;{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.E20.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E20.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{s.t.}}\;\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{E}_{m}}x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}b_{m}\leq Q_{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{s.t.}}\;\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{E}_{m}}x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}b_{m}\leq Q_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.E20.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E20.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\left\{0,1\right\},\;\forall m\in\mathcal{M},\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n,i_{m}^{\left(\ell\right)}}\in\left\{0,1\right\},\;\forall m\in\mathcal{M},\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m},i_{m}^{(\ell)}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}^{(\ell)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The objective function <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}p_{u,m}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\tilde{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}p_{u,m}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\sum_{S_{m}^{(\ell)}\in{\mathcal{A}}_{m}^{(\ell)}}p_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell">
<div id="S5.E22.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:26.1pt;vertical-align:-14.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(50.3pt,-3.8pt) scale(1.41179476590068,1.41179476590068) ;">
<p id="S5.E22.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.E22.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\bigcup_{n^{\prime}=1}^{n-1}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n^{\prime}}\right)-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\cup\left(\bigcup_{n^{\prime}=1}^{n-1}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n^{\prime}}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\bigcup_{n^{\prime}=1}^{n-1}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n^{\prime}}\right)-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\cup\left(\bigcup_{n^{\prime}=1}^{n-1}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n^{\prime}}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">That is, given the caching results of the previous edge servers from <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we aim to optimize the caching strategy of edge server <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to maximize the average reduction in latency.
Specifically, when <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{1}\right)=T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\max}-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>token</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{r}}_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{1}\right)=T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\max}-T_{u,S_{m}^{(\ell)}}^{\mathrm{token}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the objective function of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> follows from</p>
<table id="S5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\tilde{\mathbf{X}})=F\left(\bigcup_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\tilde{F}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\tilde{\mathbf{X}})=F\left(\bigcup_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\tilde{F}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The second equality holds since the sum of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a telescoping sum, where all intermediate terms cancel out, leaving only the first and the last terms.
This motivates us to divide the original problem into <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> subproblems and solve them successively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>2 </span>Subproblem analysis for <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take the subproblem <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as an example, we analyze its property and propose an efficient accelerated knapsack algorithm to solve it.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is maximizing the sum of a non-decreasing modular function and a non-decreasing supermodular function subject to a knapsack constraint. The modular function corresponds to the term including <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the supermodular function corresponds to the term including <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ V-B2 Subproblem analysis for 𝐾≥1 ‣ V-B General Case: K≥1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is omitted here because the procedure is similar to that of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ IV-B Problem Characterization ‣ IV Problem Formulation and Characterization ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, we provide an explanation about why the traditional greedy algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-A1 Algorithm design ‣ V-A Special Case: K=1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) cannot achieve a constant-approximation guarantee when solving <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Greedy Limitations in Supermodular Optimization Problems)
In MoE inference with <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, each token must activate multiple experts simultaneously within a layer, introducing strong interdependencies among the selected experts. The overall utility of a selection can only be accurately assessed once all required experts have been determined. Prior to this, the contribution of any individual expert is difficult to evaluate in isolation, often resulting in an underestimation of its true utility.
While the greedy algorithm may be effective when <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, where expert activations are independent and the utility of each expert can be evaluated individually, they fail to account for the combinatorial nature of utility when <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. In these cases, early greedy selections are made with incomplete information and may restrict the effectiveness of subsequent choices, leading to suboptimal overall performance due to cascading effects.
In contrast, the proposed method precomputes a utility score for each expert based on its isolated contribution when added to an empty set. Although the utilities are computed independently, the dynamic programming approach systematically explores the combinatorial space of expert subsets, enabling globally optimal selection. This strategy mitigates the shortsightedness inherent in greedy methods and yields higher-quality solutions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>3 </span>The proposed DP-based algorithm</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since greedy algorithm is improper to solve <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we reformulate <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> into a tractable modular optimization problem and provide solutions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)\triangleq{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)+{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>mod</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>super</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)\triangleq{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)+{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>mod</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>super</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the modular and supermodular components of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
We define a modular function as <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{H_{n}}:2^{\mathcal{N}}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{H_{n}}:2^{\mathcal{N}}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{z\in\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}(z\mid\emptyset)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>super</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)=\sum_{z\in\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}(z\mid\emptyset)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we reformulate <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}2_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}2_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}3_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}3_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be expressed as follows,</p>
<table id="S5.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E24.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E24.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}3_{n}:\mathop{\max}\limits_{\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}\;{\bar{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)={\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)+H_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">max</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>mod</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}3_{n}:\mathop{\max}\limits_{\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}}\;{\bar{F}}_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)={\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)+H_{n}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{X}}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.E24.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E24.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm{s.t.}\;(\ref{cst:user_knapsack}),(\ref{cst:user_binary})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">.</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E20.2" title="In 20 ‣ V-B1 Problem decomposition ‣ V-B General Case: K≥1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20b</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E20.3" title="In 20 ‣ V-B1 Problem decomposition ‣ V-B General Case: K≥1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20c</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm{s.t.}\;(\ref{cst:user_knapsack}),(\ref{cst:user_binary})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the objective function <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{F}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{F}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a modular function, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}3_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}3_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a general knapsack problem, which can be solved optimally with a DP-based algorithm in polynomial time. We outline the procedure in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ V-B3 The proposed DP-based algorithm ‣ V-B General Case: K≥1 ‣ V Proposed Algorithms ‣ SlimCaching: Edge Caching of Mixture-of-Experts for Distributed Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The gap between the proposed solutions and the global optimal solutions of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}1</annotation></semantics></math> will be discussed in the following paragraphs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Proposed DP-based Algorithm When <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              Expert values <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}(i\mid\emptyset)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>mod</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{mod}}(i\mid\emptyset)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}(i\mid\emptyset)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>super</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tilde{F}}_{n}^{\mathrm{super}}(i\mid\emptyset)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, expert data size <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, edge server <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>’s storage capacity <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>’s cardinality <math id="alg2.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
